  "id": "COMPOUND:31358 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Brusatol exhibits a consistent relationship with LNCaP through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is identified as a target of Hepatocyte and MOVP-3, which in turn target LNCaP, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of cellular processes in these cells. The presence of a direct target relationship between Brusatol and LNCaP, as inferred through the pathway involving (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, further supports a mechanistic link. The scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways suggests that Brusatol may influence cellular functions in LNCaP through a complex network of targets, potentially involving metabolic or signaling pathways that are yet to be fully characterized.",
